          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Oenothera humifusa, the seabeach evening primrose or spreading evening primrose, is a species of flowering plant in the family Onagraceae. It is native to the beaches of Bermuda and the eastern United States from Louisiana to New Jersey, and it has been introduced to Cuba. It is a decumbent perennial."
